<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Android 8.1 cannot reach vk.com without this.

    vk.com serves "CN=*.vk.com" signed by "Google Trust Services, CN=WR1" and sends nothing else,
    so the chain has to be completed with GTS Root R1 - which Android only ships from API 29.
    On 8.1 every player page request dies with

        SSLHandshakeException: CertPathValidatorException: Trust anchor for certification path
        not found.

    and the episode resolves to no video at all. Google usually survives this because GTS Root R1
    is cross-signed by GlobalSign Root CA (present since forever), but vk.com does not send the
    cross-signed intermediate.

    @raw/extra_ca_roots holds, in this order:

      GTS Root R1                     D9:47:43:2A:BD:E7:B7:FA:90:FC:2E:6B:59:10:1B:12:80:E0:E1:C7:E4:E4:0F:A3:C6:88:7F:FF:57:A7:F4:CF
      GTS Root R2                     8D:25:CD:97:22:9D:BF:70:35:6B:DA:4E:B3:CC:73:40:31:E2:4C:F0:0F:AF:CF:D3:2D:C7:6E:B5:84:1C:7E:A8
      GTS Root R3                     34:D8:A7:3E:E2:08:D9:BC:DB:0D:95:65:20:93:4B:4E:40:E6:94:82:59:6E:8B:6F:73:C8:42:6B:01:0A:6F:48
      GTS Root R4                     34:9D:FA:40:58:C5:E2:63:12:3B:39:8A:E7:95:57:3C:4E:13:13:C8:3F:E6:8F:93:55:6C:D5:E8:03:1B:3C:7D
      HARICA TLS ECC Root CA 2021     3F:99:CC:47:4A:CF:CE:4D:FE:D5:87:94:66:5E:47:8D:15:47:73:9F:2E:78:0F:1B:B4:CA:9B:13:30:97:D4:01
      HARICA TLS RSA Root CA 2021     D9:5D:0E:8E:DA:79:52:5B:F9:BE:B1:1B:14:D2:10:0D:32:94:98:5F:0C:62:D9:FA:BD:9C:D9:99:EC:CB:7B:1D

    Only GTS Root R1 is needed today. R2-R4 are its siblings, kept so a rotation on vk.com's side
    does not break 8.1 again. The two HARICA roots belong to vkvd*.okcdn.ru, which serves the video
    file itself - that host validates on 8.1 right now only because its 2021 root is cross-signed by
    "Hellenic Academic and Research Institutions ECC RootCA 2015", which 8.1 does have, and the
    server still sends the cross-signed copy. The vk.com breakage is exactly what happens when a
    server stops sending a cross-sign, so the real roots are carried here too.

    All six were taken from the Mozilla root bundle, not downloaded from the CAs, and the chains
    were checked against them with `openssl verify` before being added.

    "system" must stay listed: naming a certificates source replaces the default set rather than
    adding to it. cleartextTrafficPermitted must stay true as well - android:usesCleartextTraffic on
    <application> is ignored once this file exists, and shikimori hands out http:// player urls
    (http://vk.com/video_ext.php?..., http://video.sibnet.ru/...).

    This only applies from API 24. Below that Android ignores the file and vk.com stays unreachable.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
            <certificates src="@raw/extra_ca_roots" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
